The W67 Rust code is written against an "Assumed W64–W66 surface" table that contradicts the W64 code in this same plan, so the given code does not compile:
- the tests call `FluidCore::new` with 6 args, while W64 D64-4 freezes 7;
- `Elements::home_rect(id)` and `target_px(id,u,v)`, while W64 takes `reduced_motion`;
- fields `rest_hold_s` and `phase`, which W64's Elements lacks;
- `self.material` and `self.reduced_motion`, while W64 uses `settings.*`;
- `set_dirty_aabb`/`clear`, while W64 has `set_region`/`clear_region`;
- `update_rest_state` with 3 args and new `pin_to_targets`/`measure_max_dev` signatures, while W64's `redistribute()`/`refresh_rest_state` (not updated by W67.10) still call the old ones.
Step W67.1 "adapt only W67's call sites" pushes this onto the implementer.

